				<title>Mod Post</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-121418/most-recently-created#post-2094338</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 21 Aug 2014 23:32:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zyn</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1404533</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>As per staff consensus (and thanks to Gene R for bringing the matter up!) the Most Recently Created page has gotten an update.</p> <p>Now the page lists:<br /> - number of comments<br /> - most recent comment time<br /> - time of page creation<br /> - most recent edit time</p> <p>Similar to forum post timestamps (for people with computers, anyway), mousing over the dates should display a time value in minutes or hours! (For example, if you hover over the creation time of an article, the little popup display will show how many minutes or hours it's been since that time.)</p> <p>Hopefully this will be useful to all the helpful mainsite-goers who comment on new SCPs.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
